# Letters from home (prompt 08 §2, docs/story/03_cast.md). One node per letter; data/hearth/hearth.json
# says when each one arrives. Sam writes in second person, as if the letters could reach Codd.
# Short, funny first, never maudlin. Each line is one paragraph of the letter.

== letter_1 ==
Sam: You missed my birthday again. Work, I know. I ate your slice of cake, as punishment.
Sam: Mum says you are "on a long trip". I said nobody goes on a trip in their office chair.
Sam: Write back. Or don't. But eat something that is not from a machine.

== letter_2 ==
Sam: I went to your office to get your things. Your desk still has the mug I gave you.
Sam: Someone had left a sticky note on your screen: "report?". I wrote "no" under it.
Sam: The plant is alive. I am taking it home. It is mine now.
